Why GPL-3.0-only
----------------

Station Manager was MIT-licensed until 2026-05-31. It moved to
GPL-3.0-only because its FT8 decode capability is provided by the
companion library go-ft8 (github.com/ColonelBlimp/go-ft8), which is a
WSJT-X/jt9-derived work and therefore GPL-3.0-only. Linking that library
into the daemon makes the combined work a derivative of GPLv3 code, and
GPL-3.0-only's copyleft requires the whole work be distributed under the
same licence. The reasoning trail is in `docs/decisions/0023-relicense-to-gplv3.md`
and `docs/licensing.md`.

The "version 3 only" (not "or later") wording is inherited from go-ft8,
which is itself version-3-only; a work linking version-3-only code cannot
offer the "or any later version" option.

